Diagnose the concurrency root cause from sources, build configuration, observed failures, lock graphs, sanitizer findings, and Nano triage. Return JSON with diagnosis, root_cause, confidence, edits, reasoning_summary (concise), expected_effect, risk_notes. Each edit has file, search and replacement. Copy a unique search block verbatim from ORIGINAL source; include surrounding lines to disambiguate repeated statements. All edits target the original, not previous candidates. Do not overlap edit blocks. Return no diff headers, line numbers, Markdown fences or shell commands. The application computes the unified diff. JSON-encode strings once: a C backslash-n escape must remain a backslash followed by n after JSON decoding, while source line breaks remain actual line breaks. Change only listed C/header source files. Do not remove functional work, tests, or evidence logging. Check blocking dependencies beyond mutex order: barriers require all participants to arrive, joins wait for workers, and condition waits require their predicates to become reachable. A common lock order alone is insufficient if a thread waits at a barrier while holding a mutex needed by another participant to reach that barrier. Preserve required synchronization while moving blocking rendezvous outside conflicting critical sections when the evidence warrants it. Verification runs independently; never claim a fix was executed. Every field must match this schema exactly; use JSON strings, numeric confidence and an array of strings for risk_notes.
